-- title:
--   Degree-e coefficients of π v - fu relations lie in (π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, let $\pi \in W$ be non-zero, and let $f, u, v$ be formal power series in two variables over $W$ (elements of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) with $v$ a unit and with the constant coefficient of $f$, i.e. the coefficient at the zero exponent vector, equal to $0$. Fix a natural number $e$ and three further power series $g, g_1, r$ such that every coefficient of $g$ at a multi-index $n$ with $n_0 + n_1 < e$ vanishes, every coefficient of $g_1$ at a multi-index $n$ with $n_0 + n_1 < e + 1$ vanishes, and the relation $g = g_1 + (C(\pi) v - f u) r$ holds, where $C(\pi)$ is the constant power series $\pi$. Then for every multi-index $n$ with $n_0 + n_1 = e$ the coefficient of $g$ at $n$ lies in the ideal of $W$ generated by $\pi$.
--
--   This is the well-definedness statement underlying initial forms on a local chart of the Drinfeld curve: in the quotient $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\pi)v - fu)$, two representatives of the same class modulo the $(e+1)$-st power of the maximal ideal have degree-$e$ parts agreeing modulo $\pi$, so the degree-$e$ initial form of an element of the $e$-th power of the maximal ideal is well defined over the residue characteristic. It is used in the chart-ring computations that identify the image of the variables and the Drinfeld form in terms of their linear parts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_coeff_mem_span_of_eq_add_rel_mul_of_forall_coeff_eq_zero.lean

